.Dd October 29, 2026
.Dt ARCH 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm arch
.Nd print the architecture, or run a program for one
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Nm
.Oo Fl Ns Ar arch_name | Fl arch Ar arch_name Oc ...
.Op Fl c
.Op Fl d Ar envname
.Op Fl e Ar envname Ns = Ns Ar value
.Op Fl h
.Ar prog
.Op Ar args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
With no arguments,
.Nm
prints the machine's architecture family:
.Ql i386
on Intel machines, whether 32- or 64-bit.
.Pp
With a program,
.Nm
runs it, choosing from a universal binary the first of the architectures
given that it holds:
.Cm i386 ,
.Cm x86_64 ,
.Cm x86_64h ,
.Cm arm64
or
.Cm arm64e .
The program must be able to run on this machine.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl c
Run it with an empty environment.
.It Fl d Ar envname
Remove
.Ar envname
from its environment.
.It Fl e Ar envname Ns = Ns Ar value
Set
.Ar envname
in its environment.
.It Fl h
Print a summary of the options.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
With a program, its exit status; otherwise 0, or 1 on an error.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr uname 1 ,
.Xr posix_spawnattr_setbinpref_np 3
.Sh HISTORY
Minkar's
.Nm
is its own.
